!In lieu of a single Lojban/English dictionary, there are several word lists for  the different grammatical classes.

'''cmavo'''
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/cmavo.txt|alphabet order]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/cmavo_variant_order.txt|alphabet order with vowels first] (the file is missing; here's [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/cmavo_variant_order.txt,D|what seems to be a diff between the file and nothing])
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/cmavo_variant_order.txt|strange order] (same as above)
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/cmavo_selmaho_order.txt|in selma'o order]

'''gismu'''
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/gismu.txt|alphabet order]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/gismu_english_order.txt|English keyword order]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/oblique_keywords.txt|keywords for non-x1 gismu places]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/oldlog.txt|mapping to old Loglan "prims"]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/roget.txt|Roget's thesaurus codes]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/gismu_spanish.txt|alphabet order with Spanish translations]
* (( [http://www.thestonecutters.net/xod/lojban/gismu-thesaurus.html|Gismu Thesaurus ))] ''(Ignore the gismu links!)''
* ((Format of Gismu Lists))

'''lujvo'''
* [http://www.lojban.org/files/draft-dictionary/NORALUJV.txt|"current"]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/lujvo.txt|old]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/lujvo_old.txt|older]
* [http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/lujvo_ancient.txt|ancient]

((Word frequency lists)).

----
!!!There are also web-based dictionaries that perform dynamic word searches in English and Lojban.

* [http://www.animal.helsinki.fi/lojban/gismu-search-form.html|gismu dictionary]
* [http://valfahi.balvi.org/|valfa'i, which searches gismu, cmavo, and lujvo]

----
[http://www.rrbcurnow.freeuk.com/lojban/index.html|Richard Curnow's Lojban dictionary] might also be interesting -- 24 pages of small print with information on gismu, rafsi, cmavo, the grammar, etc. The dictionary itself is available in [http://www.rrbcurnow.freeuk.com/lojban/dict.pdf|Adobe PDF] and [http://www.rrbcurnow.freeuk.com/lojban/dict.ps.gz|gzipped PostScript] formats. --mi'e ((pne|filip))

----
''To whomever making this page, thanks a lot! I had lost all my "dictionary"-files after a harddisk crash and could no longer find all these precious word-lists on the net, since the official Lojban site had been moved and re-written.  (The different main lists all put together into one text file and running this with BBEdit seems to be a pretty comfortable word lookup tool!)  -- .aulun. ''
